            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kourtneyrabi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tried this recipe last night for a girl 's night out potluck. The others and I really liked it. I did boil the rhubarb with maybe a teaspoon of sugar, and I added strawberries, about 2 cups of them as well. I also mixed the batter and the fruit together mainly because I like fruit dispersed throughout my baked goods. If I hadn't mixed them, I would have served it like an upside down cake. Overall god recipe and I will try it again with peaches since they are now in season.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-02T14:09:36.853Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ChileDog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used blackberries (and 2 Tbsp sugar) for the fruit, but followed the topping recipe exactly. It came out beautifully. Really simple, but delicious. More cake-like than cobbler -- would work well with most fruit. Highly recommend!",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-21T14:54:05.013Z"
